<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 1.3 · Bird Runs & Infrastructure" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="1-3" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 1.3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Turn the cash pile into permanent account infrastructure.</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">This is the densest subsection in Chapter 1. The route finishes Mage Training Arena in one sitting, builds the Crafting/teleport network, unlocks Fossil Island and birdhouse runs, finishes the important quest foundation needed by the rest of Chapter 1, unlocks fairy rings, and closes with the Zeah quest block before the long Woodcutting break in 1.4.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="By the end of 1.3 the account should have Bones to Peaches permanently unlocked, 1,600 buckets of sand converted into 1,600 molten glass, the 7-piece quest-glass reserve protected, and the 1,590-unpowered-orb grind either finished or underway. It should also have 2,000 stardust banked for Chapter 2, 44 Mining / actual 46+ Crafting to blow orbs / 46+ Fletching, Fossil Island and birdhouses running, fairy-ring access, The Fremennik Trials complete, 60% Tai Bwo Wannai favour for My Arm, and enough quest-awarded Farming XP to start Garden of Tranquillity immediately in 1.4. Finish the orb stock in 1.4, claim its Crafting quests, then check live XP before deciding on a battlestaff boost or permanent level."
        stats={["44 Mining + 2,000 banked stardust", "Actual 46 Crafting before orb-blowing; live XP afterward, not a promised 56", "46+ Fletching deliberately; roughly 47–48 by Chapter 1 end depending on Wintertodt/incidental XP", "At least 33 Farming before 1.4", "31 Herblore before Eadgar's Ruse in 1.4", "Hunter progressing passively through birdhouses"]}
        unlocks={["Bones to Peaches", "1,590 unpowered orbs + the reserved quest glass for the Chapter 1 Earth-orb route", "Fossil Island / mushtrees / birdhouse runs", "Fairy rings", "Rune sword + green d'hide starter gear", "The Fremennik Trials", "Death Plateau + Troll Stronghold", "60% Tai Bwo Wannai favour for My Arm", "Zeah quest foundation"]}
      />

      <RouteStep id="i13-runes" number="1" title="Buy the Mage Training Arena rune stock to explicit bank totals">
        <p>First check <strong>actual Magic</strong>. Train to at least <strong>33</strong> for Telekinetic Grab, then to <strong>actual 54</strong> before the Lvl-4 Enchant room: a Wizard's mind bomb supplies the remaining +3 to cast the level-57 spell. Use ordinary elemental combat spells on safe, low-defence targets and buy only the runes for the live XP gap; keep the MTA law/nature/cosmic stock separate. MTA awards Magic XP too, but neither the Chapter 1.2 exit nor its rune purchases guaranteed these spell levels. If your account already has 54, skip this bridge.</p>
        <p>For the MTA runes, use <strong>Lundail's shop inside the Mage Arena bank in deep Wilderness</strong> and bring your bank to at least:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>1,650 nature runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>700 law runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>500 chaos runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>400 cosmic runes</strong></li>
          <li><strong>500 water runes</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Do not carry the full 1.35m through Wilderness.</strong> Bank your valuable kit and coins before the dangerous approach, bring only disposable travel gear, and withdraw purchase money after reaching the safe Mage Arena bank. The bank/shop is safe, but the route to it is not; Hardcore players can instead complete The Feud plus Rogue Trader's rune-shop section and buy from Ali Morrisane in Al Kharid at a higher price. Buy an <strong>air staff, earth staff and fire staff</strong> from <strong>Zaff in Varrock</strong> if missing, plus <strong>10 Wizard's mind bombs</strong> from Falador's Rising Sun Inn. These are MTA opening totals, not a promise of leftover alchemy runes: buy small top-ups if your point route consumes more than estimated.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-mta" number="2" title="Finish Mage Training Arena now and unlock Bones to Peaches">
        <p><strong>The entire reason for MTA here is Bones to Peaches.</strong> The spell costs <strong>200 Telekinetic, 300 Alchemist, 2,000 Enchantment and 200 Graveyard pizazz points</strong>. Finish the unlock in this visit so MTA does not remain an open chore for the next ten hours.</p>
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Use these buffered point targets and room loops:</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Graveyard — 211 points:</strong> take bones from a pile, cast <strong>Bones to Bananas</strong>, deposit the bananas in the chute, and eat bananas when you need healing. Repeat until the point target is reached.</li>
            <li><strong>Telekinetic — 211 points:</strong> position yourself on the side of the maze that pulls the guardian toward the next opening, then cast <strong>Telekinetic Grab</strong>. Complete each maze rather than abandoning it halfway through.</li>
            <li><strong>Alchemist — 311 points:</strong> the cabinet values rotate. Alch the item currently worth <strong>30 coins</strong>; ignore poor-value items. Low Alchemy works. If a Wizard's Mind Bomb gives you High Alchemy, use it for faster casts.</li>
            <li><strong>Enchantment — 2,165 points:</strong> use the highest enchantment spell you can cast reliably. With the route's level range, <strong>Lvl-4 Enchant</strong> with a Wizard's Mind Bomb is the intended option. Prioritize the current bonus shape/corner, enchant shapes, then drop them after they score.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p>At the rewards shop, buy <strong>1 mud rune</strong> and <strong>10 mist runes</strong>, then buy <strong>Bones to Peaches</strong>. The unlock requires <strong>60 Magic, boostable</strong>: check your actual level after the room XP, train only any remainder to <strong>actual 57</strong>, then use a Wizard's mind bomb for +3 if needed. When the spell is unlocked, MTA is finished for Chapter 1. <strong>Record your remaining nature runes:</strong> MTA consumes much of the opening stock, and 2.1 will audit and replenish to 1,590 for High Alchemy rather than counting these same runes twice.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-quest-foundation" number="3" title="Finish the missing early quest foundation before the infrastructure grind">
        <p>Complete these as standalone quests, in this order:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Demon Slayer</strong></li>
          <li><strong>A Porcine of Interest</strong> — the 1,000 Slayer XP combines with the Varrock Museum Natural History Quiz to comfortably clear Desert Treasure's 10 Slayer requirement.</li>
          <li><strong>Vampyre Slayer</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Below Ice Mountain</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Golem</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Shadow of the Storm</strong> — put the selectable <strong>10,000 combat XP into Ranged</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Lost Tribe</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Enter the Abyss</strong> miniquest — finish it completely so Abyss access is unlocked</li>
          <li><strong>Merlin's Crystal</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Dig Site</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Elemental Workshop I</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Elemental Workshop II</strong> — if you are still below 30 Smithing, use Giant Foundry or ordinary bars to reach 30 first</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Before Shadow of the Storm:</strong> check that one of the quest-reserved silver bars from 1.1 remains for its crafted demonic sigil. If it was spent, buy one replacement from the East Ardougne Silver Merchant before this quest; do not count optional jewellery as a replacement. This block restores several quests that the high-efficiency route touches in fragments. Here they are simply finished. <strong>The Dig Site</strong> is especially important because it feeds both Fossil Island and Desert Treasure; <strong>Enter the Abyss</strong> is kept because it is a permanent Runecraft/travel unlock rather than diary-only routing.</p>
        <p>By this point you are comfortably over <strong>32 Quest Points</strong>. Go upstairs in the <strong>Champions' Guild</strong> and buy from <strong>Scavvo</strong>:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>1 rune sword</strong> — specifically the rune <em>sword</em>, not the rune longsword</li>
          <li><strong>1 green d'hide chaps</strong></li>
          <li><strong>1 green d'hide vambraces</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Keep all three. The rune sword is the simple melee weapon used through the rest of Chapter 1 and early Chapter 2, and the green d'hide is useful early Ranged/quest gear.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="The twelve foundation quests: supplies and recovery">
          <p><strong>Rebank between quests.</strong> The quantities below are per quest; a bar, loaf or vial handed in earlier is already spent. Use the <a href="#i13-quest-supplies">material suppliers below</a> for missing basics, and bring food plus a bank teleport for fights.</p>
          <ul>
          <li><strong>Demon Slayer:</strong> 1 coin, a bucket of water and <strong>25 unnoted ordinary bones</strong>. Kill chickens/cows and bank the bones until you have 25; ashes and big bones do not substitute. The three keys and Silverlight come from the quest. Keep Silverlight for Shadow of the Storm.</li>
          <li><strong>A Porcine of Interest:</strong> 1 rope, a knife or suitable slash weapon, combat gear and food. Buy rope from Ned in Draynor; a knife avoids relying on whether your weapon can cut the vines.</li>
          <li><strong>Vampyre Slayer:</strong> hammer and 2 coins for Morgan's requested beer at Varrock's Blue Moon Inn. Dr Harlow supplies the stake after the dialogue; carry it and the hammer during the fight.</li>
          <li><strong>Below Ice Mountain:</strong> 1 cooked meat, 1 bread, knife and 3 coins. Buy raw beef and flour from Wydin in Port Sarim, cook the beef and make bread; do not substitute chicken or fish for cooked meat. The quest provides its other sandwich ingredients.</li>
          <li><strong>The Golem:</strong> 4 soft clay, 1 empty vial, pestle and mortar and 1 papyrus. Buy papyrus from Aemad in East Ardougne; mine four clay south-west of Varrock and soften with water. Collect the phoenix feather and black mushrooms during the quest.</li>
          <li><strong>Shadow of the Storm:</strong> Silverlight, 1 separate silver bar, 3 accepted dark clothing items, combat runes and food. Buy priest gown top and bottom from Thessalia in Varrock and a black wizard hat from Betty in Port Sarim; ordinary dark-looking gear is not automatically accepted. The Golem's black-mushroom area supplies the ink to dye Silverlight. Use the quest mould and silver bar at a furnace for the demonic sigil; Silverlight must deal the finishing blow.</li>
          <li><strong>The Lost Tribe:</strong> pickaxe, lit candle and tinderbox. Buy a candle from Catherby's candle shop if missing. Use the castle-cellar route and stay on the quest's marked cave path; a candle is not safe for exploring swamp gas elsewhere. Keep the quest's brooch and notes until its dialogue has consumed them.</li>
          <li><strong>Enter the Abyss:</strong> no outside quest ingredient is consumed. The Mage of Zamorak supplies the scrying orb; carry it to the three required essence-mine teleports. Bank valuables before meeting him in low Wilderness, then continue his Varrock-chaos-temple dialogue.</li>
          <li><strong>Merlin's Crystal:</strong> 1 fresh bread, tinderbox, empty bucket and combat gear. Take insect repellent from the Catherby house north of the bank, then use the bucket on the beehives for wax. Kill a bat near Keep Le Faye for bat bones; the quest supplies Excalibur. Keep that sword for Holy Grail.</li>
          <li><strong>The Dig Site:</strong> 2 ropes, 1 empty vial, pestle and mortar, tinderbox and 1 cup of tea from the Varrock tea stall. A cut or uncut opal can be obtained by panning at the Digsite, and charcoal by searching its specimen trays. Collect the exam/panning tools there; no Shilo Village gem access is needed.</li>
          <li><strong>Elemental Workshop I:</strong> knife, pickaxe, hammer, needle, thread, soft leather and <strong>4 coal</strong>. Tan one cowhide into soft leather at Ellis in Al Kharid; buy needle/thread at Dommik nearby. Mine coal at 30 Mining, or buy it from Ordan after the first boat trip into Keldagrim (that trip starts The Giant Dwarf; finish it at Step 13). Keep the battered key and elemental shield.</li>
          <li><strong>Elemental Workshop II:</strong> the same pickaxe/hammer/key and <strong>8 new coal</strong>. Check actual 30 Smithing before starting; the earlier four coal are spent. If the key is lost, search the bookcase in the house south of the Seers' Village workshop, then use a knife on the battered book. Make and retain the mind helmet/shield as the quest directs.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <div id="i13-quest-supplies">
          <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Reusable suppliers for this chapter's missing materials">
            <p><strong>Check the bank first, then buy or make only the shortfall.</strong> Use the liquid-cash refill from Chapter 1.2 if purchases exceed the remaining coins; projected alchemy value is not spendable cash. Quantities in a quest's note are its own allocation, after previous uses.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Tools and containers:</strong> general stores such as Lumbridge's sell hammer, chisel, tinderbox, buckets and pots. Take a knife from the Lumbridge Castle kitchen/cellar spawn or buy one from Ardougne's spice seller. Dommik in Al Kharid sells needle, thread, jewellery/sickle/holy moulds; the Varrock Sawmill sells saws and nails. Ned in Draynor sells rope; buy balls of wool from Aemad's Adventuring Supplies in East Ardougne, or shear sheep north of Lumbridge and spin their wool at the castle's first-floor spinning wheel (1 Crafting). Sarah's farm shop south of Falador sells farming tools, plant pots, compost and cure. Buy an empty item when the quest asks for empty; fill water containers at a sink or fountain.</li>
              <li><strong>Bars and wire:</strong> use a furnace to smelt one copper + one tin into bronze (1 Smithing), iron ore into iron (15, with failed smelts possible), or one iron + two coal into steel (30). Smith one bronze bar into one bronze wire at 4 Smithing. Mine the basic ore south-east/south-west of Varrock; coal requires 30 Mining, or buy it from Ordan after the boat into Keldagrim. Gold needs 40 Smithing. The first Keldagrim boat trip starts The Giant Dwarf automatically; shopping there does not complete the quest.</li>
              <li><strong>Planks / leather / clay / glass:</strong> cut the required tree and pay the Varrock Sawmill to convert its logs into the named plank tier. Kill a cow and pay Ellis in Al Kharid for <em>soft</em> or <em>hard</em> leather as specified. Mine clay south-west of Varrock and add water for soft clay. Charter traders sell buckets of sand and soda ash; smelt one of each at a furnace for one molten glass. Take a glassblowing pipe from the house west of Entrana's furnace (bank weapons/armour before the boat) and use it on the glass for the required item. Extra quest glass uses a fresh recipe, not the protected 1,600-piece orb allocation.</li>
              <li><strong>Food ingredients:</strong> Wydin in Port Sarim sells flour, redberries and raw beef/chicken. Water + flour makes bread dough; bake it on a range. For a redberry pie, make pastry dough, put it in a pie dish, add redberries and bake at 10 Cooking; a pie dish spawns in Varrock Palace's kitchen. Milk a dairy cow with an empty bucket and collect eggs at Lumbridge farms. Repeat if food burns. Ordinary cooked fish for travel can come from the Fishing bank or a short Catherby catch-and-cook refill.</li>
              <li><strong>Low-level herbs:</strong> preserve actual banked herbs first. If a named marrentill, tarromin, harralander or ranarr is missing, take combat gear, food and a bank teleport to the chaos druids near the entrance of Taverley Dungeon. Bank the matching herb drops until the requested quantity is met; no fixed kill count or Wintertodt yield is assumed. Sanfew in Taverley sells water-filled vials and pestle and mortar. Clean the herb at its Herblore level, or pay Zahur in Nardah 200 coins per herb if the requested clean herb is above your level. A herb added to water is an <strong>unfinished</strong> potion, not a finished combat potion.</li>
              <li><strong>Enclosed light when a cave needs it:</strong> at 26 Smithing, smith one extra iron bar into an oil-lantern frame. Blow one freshly sourced molten glass into an oil lamp at 12 Crafting, then combine frame and lamp at 26 Crafting. Pick up one swamp tar in Lumbridge Swamp, use it on the Chemist's lamp-oil still west of Rimmington, fill the lantern and light it with a tinderbox at 26 Firemaking. This gives an <strong>oil lantern</strong>, not an exposed oil lamp; carry the tinderbox in case it goes out. If below a crafting/smithing gate, bridge only that live gap with ordinary glass/bars before a quest requires the enclosed light. Candles are adequate only where the quest note specifically uses them.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Quest-supplied keys, moulds, letters and special plants stay with the quest until its steps consume them. Ordinary ingredient deficits are solved here; a missing special quest item is recovered from its named NPC/container in Quest Helper rather than bought from an unrelated shop.</p>
          </ExpandableNote>
        </div>

      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-sand" number="4" title="Mine the 1,600 buckets of sand first; then finish Mining at Shooting Stars">
        <p><strong>This is a resource step first and a Mining-XP step second.</strong> Withdraw a pickaxe, desert clothing, waterskins/food, about <strong>80,000 gp</strong>, and the <strong>1,600 noted empty buckets</strong> banked in 1.2. Go to the <strong>Desert Quarry / Sandstorm grinder</strong> and give the noted buckets to <strong>Drew</strong>.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Mine sandstone and deposit every piece into <strong>Sandstorm</strong>.</li>
          <li>Continue until the grinder is holding enough processed sand for <strong>1,600 buckets</strong>. Sand yield depends on sandstone size, so the target is the grinder total—not 1,600 individual rocks.</li>
          <li>Pay Drew <strong>50 gp per bucket</strong> and withdraw exactly <strong>1,600 buckets of sand</strong>. That costs <strong>80,000 gp</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Mining-level choice:</strong> staying at sandstone until roughly <strong>43 Mining</strong> matches the source route and gets most of the level quickly. If the 1,600-sand resource target is already finished and you are tired of the desert, leave immediately and finish the level at Shooting Stars instead.</p>
        <p>After the sand is banked, use <strong>tier 4 or lower Shooting Stars</strong> with your <strong>best available pickaxe</strong> for the relaxed route; use a rune pickaxe if you already have one. Continue until you have both <strong>44 Mining</strong> and <strong>2,000 total stardust</strong>. If 44 Mining comes first, keep mining stars until 2,000 stardust. <strong>Do not spend the stardust:</strong> early Chapter 2 buys the Celestial ring with all 2,000.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Crafting gate before the method panel:</strong> the already-completed mandatory quests give at least <strong>22,950 Crafting XP</strong> before this glass block (level 35). Furnace-smelting 1,600 glass adds <strong>32,000 XP</strong>, giving a conservative <strong>54,950 XP (level 43)</strong> before any extra Crafting or jewellery. Unpowered orbs need <strong>actual 46 Crafting (67,983 XP)</strong>, so read live XP after smelting and fill only the gap with banked gems or separately sourced extra sand/soda ash and glass. Do not spend the protected 1,600-glass allocation on that bridge. Later orb XP starts from the post-smelting level-46 checkpoint; the 32,000 XP must not be added a second time.</div>

<TrainingOptions id="i13-crafting-training" skill="Crafting" target="actual 46 before blowing; protect 1,590 orbs" why="Blowing 1,590 unpowered orbs gives 83,475 Crafting XP, but this is a resource goal, not proof of level 56 or 58. The live XP entering the orb block varies with earlier extra training and jewellery." recommended="At a furnace, turn 1,600 soda ash + 1,600 buckets of sand into 1,600 molten glass. Immediately reserve 6 glass for Desert Treasure, 1 for the Hand in the Sand lantern lens and 1 for the birdhouse crafting table. At actual 46+ Crafting, blow exactly 1,590 of the rest into unpowered orbs. Leave any later Crafting decision until after Chapter 1.4's guaranteed quest rewards." relaxed="You do not have to blow all 1,590 orbs in one sitting. Bankstand a few hundred at a time between quests and birdhouse runs, but have enough orb XP for actual 49 before The Hand in the Sand and finish the full stack before charging Earth orbs in 1.4." resource="The accounting is intentional: 1,600 molten glass = 1,590 unpowered orbs + 6 Desert Treasure + 1 Hand in the Sand lens + 1 birdhouse crafting table 2 + 2 spare. Additional Crafting uses separately obtained materials." fast="Multiskilling glassblowing during movement is optional; plain bankstanding is the intended route." />

<TrainingOptions id="i13-fletching-training" skill="Fletching" target="46 deliberately; do not grind 48 just to match the end-of-chapter number" why="This corrects an ambiguity in the source route: BRUHsailer deliberately establishes 46 Fletching from the early arrow supply. Its roughly 48 Fletching at the end of Chapter 1 is an expected result after additional incidental and quest XP, not a special unlock. There is no Chapter 1 quest or item that suddenly requires 48. The useful future breakpoints are 50 Fletching for Devious Minds/Kandarin Medium, 52 for broad arrows (after the Slayer unlock) and The Final Dawn, and 60 for Sins of the Father; getting the cheap early arrow XP now simply reduces those later grinds." recommended="First check your level. If you are already 46+ from Wintertodt, do nothing. Otherwise use the banked oak logs set aside for Fletching: cut each oak log into 30 arrow shafts, add 30 feathers to make headless arrows, then add 30 steel arrowtips to make steel arrows. One oak log taken all the way through this chain is about 190 Fletching XP, so only process as many logs/arrows as your current XP requires to reach 46. Buy extra feathers from Gerrant's Fishy Business in Port Sarim and steel arrowtips from Hickton's Archery Emporium in Catherby; buying about 250 arrowtips per world keeps the shop price reasonable." relaxed="Bankstand the entire arrow chain in ordinary Make-X batches. There is no need to fletch while walking. Once you hit 46, stop and let later quests/passive Fletching do the rest. The Fremennik Trials awards 2,812 Fletching XP and Temple of Ikov later awards another 8,000, so your displayed level will continue rising without a dedicated 48 grind." resource="This is an XP checkpoint, not an ammunition quota: a player already at 46 may make no arrows, and someone just below it may make only a small batch. Chapter 1.4 checks the finished-arrow bank separately before training Ranged. Do not cut logs reserved for birdhouses, diaries, Sleeping Giants, Enakhra's Lament, Icthlarin's Little Helper or other named quest uses." fast="If you enjoy multiskilling, making the headless/steel arrows while travelling is faster overall, but this Intermediate route never assumes it." />

      <RouteStep id="i13-jewelry" number="5" title="Make the Chapter 1 teleport-jewelry network">
        <p><strong>Unlock digsite pendants before enchanting ruby necklaces.</strong> After The Dig Site, clean uncleaned finds in the Varrock Museum until you uncover a <strong>clean necklace</strong> (random; keep cleaning until it appears). Show it to an archaeologist in the cleaning area to learn the special Lvl-3 Enchant recipe. Then make/enchant the ruby necklaces at <strong>49 Magic</strong>, already cleared by the MTA preflight. Ordinary ruby-necklace enchantment does not automatically work before this unlock; count any Kudos earned here toward Step 6.</p>
        <p>Once your Crafting level allows it, make at least the following working stack:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>20 rings of dueling</strong></li>
          <li><strong>10 digsite pendants</strong></li>
          <li><strong>10 games necklaces</strong></li>
          <li><strong>5 necklaces of passage if jade and silver are already banked</strong>; otherwise defer this convenience stock</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The full Chapter 1 target is <strong>40 rings of dueling, 45 digsite pendants and 10 games necklaces</strong>, plus <strong>8 bracelets of clay, 2 sapphire amulets, 1 ruby amulet and 1 binding necklace</strong>. From an empty jewelry bank this is <strong>107 gold bars, 41 emeralds, 46 rubies and 20 sapphires</strong>; the five separate jade passage necklaces take <strong>five additional silver bars</strong> if chosen. Never spend the remaining quest-reserved silver bars on those optional necklaces. Count finished pieces and gems before sourcing anything. Wintertodt/Tempoross rewards are variable, not a guarantee. For missing precious gems before Shilo Village, keep the <strong>2,000 stardust reserved for the Celestial ring</strong> untouched and mine extra Shooting Stars for the low-attention route: each additional <strong>300 stardust</strong> buys a 40-gem bag from Dusuri at the Mining Guild entrance. Contents vary, so open bags and stop at the live shortfall; do not project a fixed bag count. Alternatively, the East Ardougne gem merchant sells stocked cut sapphire, emerald and ruby gems, but its low per-world stock makes a large refill repetitive. For missing gold bars, buy only the required gold ore from <strong>Ordan at Blast Furnace in Keldagrim</strong> or mine it; if below 40 Smithing, finish that conditional smelting gate with ordinary iron/steel work, then smelt gold at a furnace or Blast Furnace. Jade is <em>not</em> supplied by those star bags: if absent, leave passage necklaces for Shilo Village gem rocks after the quest in 2.2 and use ordinary travel in the meantime.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Moulds, wool and enchantment runes">
          <p>Buy ring, necklace, amulet and bracelet moulds from <strong>Dommik in Al Kharid</strong>. Use cut gems and gold bars at a furnace; amulets additionally need one <strong>ball of wool each</strong> before enchanting. Aemad's Adventuring Supplies in East Ardougne sells balls of wool, or shear sheep north of Lumbridge and spin their wool at Lumbridge Castle's first-floor wheel (1 Crafting). Necklaces and rings do not require wool.</p>
          <p>Enchant only the pieces being made: Lvl-1 Enchant uses <strong>1 cosmic + 1 water</strong> per sapphire item, Lvl-2 uses <strong>1 cosmic + 3 air</strong> per emerald item, and Lvl-3 uses <strong>1 cosmic + 5 fire</strong> per ruby item. Equip the matching elemental staff to cover those elemental runes. Buy cosmic shortfalls from Ali Morrisane's unlocked rune shop or Lundail using the travel precautions in Step 1; the MTA balance is not an untouched enchanting reserve. Bracelets of clay use <strong>sapphire bracelets</strong> and Lvl-1 Enchant; the binding necklace uses an emerald necklace. The eight bracelet sapphires are already included in the 20-sapphire total.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-fossil" number="6" title="Reach 100 Varrock Museum Kudos, complete Bone Voyage, and unlock Fossil Island">
        <p>Complete <strong>Priest in Peril</strong> first. Then go to the <strong>Varrock Museum</strong> and make the 100-Kudos requirement explicit rather than assuming it happened in the background:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Complete the <strong>Natural History Quiz</strong> in the museum basement if you have not already. Take the Hunter and Slayer XP.</li>
          <li>Talk to <strong>Historian Minas</strong> and tell him about every completed quest he will accept for Kudos.</li>
          <li>Check your total. If you are below <strong>100 Kudos</strong>, use the museum cleaning area and complete unidentified-cleaned-find displays until the total reaches at least 100.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Once the museum shows <strong>100+ Kudos</strong>, complete <strong>Bone Voyage</strong>. On Fossil Island, build the camp facilities you can build and unlock the <strong>Mushroom Meadow, Verdant Valley and House on the Hill mushtrees</strong>.</p>
        <p>Use a <strong>digsite pendant</strong> on the strange machine in the House on the Hill so future pendants can teleport there directly. While you are already on the island, mine and bank at least <strong>1,000 volcanic ash</strong>; this becomes ultracompost later.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Priest in Peril, Bone Voyage and the first camp bank">
          <ul>
          <li><strong>Priest in Peril:</strong> empty bucket, combat supplies and <strong>50 unnoted rune or pure essence</strong>. Mine any deficit using Aubury's Varrock essence teleport after Rune Mysteries; deliver it in multiple trips. Keep the bucket for the blessed-water sequence.</li>
          <li><strong>Bone Voyage:</strong> <strong>2 vodka + 1 marrentill potion (unf)</strong>. Buy vodka from Heckel Funch in the Grand Tree. Put one clean marrentill in a vial of water at 5 Herblore; do not add unicorn horn dust. If no herb remains, use the herb recovery below. The Apothecary makes the potion of sealegs from these ingredients after the quest dialogue.</li>
          <li><strong>Fossil Island camp:</strong> prioritise the bank chest with <strong>2 oak planks, 1 iron bar, 5 nails, hammer and saw</strong> at 21 Construction. Buy saw/nails and convert two cut oak logs at the Varrock Sawmill if missing. If below 21, do the Construction catch-up immediately below first. Other camp facilities are optional conveniences; they are not a condition for birdhouse runs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Wear leather gloves and leather boots and collect the trowel, rock pick and specimen brush from the museum's tool rack for cleaning finds. Buy replacement gloves/boots from a general or clothing shop rather than assuming combat vambraces work. Bring a pickaxe for the volcanic-ash stop; the 1,000-ash target is separate from the quest inventory.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <TrainingOptions id="i13-construction-training" skill="Construction" target="26 before birdhouses and Getting Ahead" why="An Ironman needs a level-25 crafting table 2 in the POH to make four clockworks from steel bars; Getting Ahead then needs actual 26 Construction. Wintertodt repair XP is variable, so check the live level before either activity." recommended="If below 20, use ordinary POH furniture with banked normal planks to reach the Novice Mahogany Homes gate. Then take Novice contracts with banked oak planks until actual 26, checking the skill tab." relaxed="Split the contracts across quest/birdhouse breaks after the first clockworks are made." resource="Use banked planks first and convert only the shortfall; reserve named quest planks." fast="Ordinary oak POH furniture is faster but uses more planks." />

      <RouteStep id="i13-birdhouses" number="7" title="Start birdhouse runs with one repeatable recipe">
        <p><strong>Make the first four clockworks:</strong> at actual <strong>25+ Construction</strong>, add a POH workshop if needed, build <strong>crafting table 1 with four oak planks</strong>, then upgrade it to <strong>crafting table 2 with one molten glass</strong> from the specifically reserved crafting-table glass. A new workshop costs <strong>10,000 coins</strong>; buy the four oak planks by converting oak logs at the sawmill if needed. Use <strong>four steel bars</strong> on the table (one per clockwork). Check for banked bars first; smelt any shortfall from iron ore and coal. The clockworks return when you harvest completed bird houses, so these are not four new bars every run.</p>
        <p><strong>Bring each run:</strong> a hammer, chisel, <strong>4 clockworks</strong>, <strong>4 logs for the highest birdhouse tier you can currently make</strong>, <strong>40 cheap bait seeds</strong>, and a digsite pendant. Low-level hop seeds such as barley or hammerstone from <strong>Olivia's Draynor Seed Market</strong> remain an easy default; eligible flower and allotment seeds also work. Keep seeds reserved for named crops and quests out of the birdhouses. Ten low-level seeds fill each house, so buy or use only enough for the houses you actually plan to set rather than assuming a fixed daily run.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Use each clockwork on a log to make <strong>4 bird houses</strong>.</li>
          <li>Teleport to the <strong>House on the Hill</strong>.</li>
          <li>Mushtree to <strong>Verdant Valley</strong> and place the two bird houses there.</li>
          <li>Mushtree to <strong>Mushroom Meadow</strong>, place the bird house there, then run south to the <strong>Tar Swamp entrance</strong> and place the fourth.</li>
          <li>Use <strong>10 cheap seeds on each bird house</strong>.</li>
          <li>After roughly <strong>50 minutes</strong>, harvest all four. You get the clockworks back; bring four replacement logs and another 40 seeds next run.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Scheduling rule:</strong> do birdhouses when you log in, finish a quest, or want a two-minute break. The route wants passive Hunter XP; it does not require alarm-clock efficiency.</div>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Chapter 2 teak preparation:</strong> save the <strong>first 2 teak seeds</strong> you receive from bird nests/contracts. Do not spend them elsewhere. You cannot plant them until <strong>35 Farming</strong>; 1.4 will tell you exactly when to turn them into saplings and start the roughly three-day growth timer.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-rfd" number="8" title="Finish the early Recipe for Disaster block in one sitting">
        <p>If <strong>Cook's Assistant</strong> is not complete, finish it first. Start <strong>Recipe for Disaster</strong>, finish the opening cook section, then complete these three subquests one at a time:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Freeing the Goblin generals</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Freeing the Mountain Dwarf</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Freeing Pirate Pete</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Pirate Pete item check:</strong> bring an empty fishbowl for the diving apparatus. If none is banked, blow one from <strong>one of the two spare molten glass</strong> at your already-verified 46+ Crafting (42 Crafting is needed); this uses 42.5 Crafting XP and still leaves the other spare glass protected for Chapter 2. Do not take a glass from the 1,590 orbs or named quest reserves.</p>
        <p>Your 1.2 quest work and 60 Cooking make this a clean time to close all three rather than starting them and carrying their ingredients through half the chapter. <strong>Freeing the Mountain Dwarf awards 1,000 Slayer XP.</strong> Combined with the 1,000 XP from A Porcine of Interest and 1,000 XP from the Varrock Museum Natural History Quiz, the route now guarantees <strong>3,000 Slayer XP (level 16)</strong>. Part 1.4 will use one short Slayer assignment to close the remaining 523 XP to level 18 before Animal Magnetism.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="RFD opening, Goblins, Mountain Dwarf and Pirate Pete">
          <p><strong>Opening cook:</strong> 1 eye of newt from Betty in Port Sarim, 1 Greenman's ale from Yanille's Dragon Inn, 1 rotten tomato from the crate by Varrock's pillory, ashes from a burnt log, and a <strong>fruit blast you make yourself</strong>. Buy a cocktail shaker, cocktail glass, 1 pineapple, 2 lemons and 1 orange from the Grand Tree's cocktail/grocery shops; mix a fruit blast in the shaker, pour it, and garnish with a slice cut from the second lemon using a knife. Then add the ashes for the dirty blast. A premade fruit blast does not work.</p>
          <ul>
          <li><strong>Goblin generals:</strong> fresh bread, orange, knife, blue/green/purple dye, spice or gnome spice, fishing bait, bucket of water and charcoal. Buy orange/spice from the Grand Tree or unlocked Culinaromancer's Chest, bait from Gerrant, charcoal from Jiminua. For a new blue dye, pay Wyson in Falador Park 20 coins for 2 woad leaves, then give both leaves and 5 coins to Aggie in Draynor. Prepare the unusual coloured/soggy food during the subquest.</li>
          <li><strong>Mountain Dwarf:</strong> 320 coins, bucket of milk, pot of flour, egg, bowl of water and 4 Asgarnian ales (buy the ales from Kaylee in Falador's Rising Sun Inn). The unlocked chest sells milk/flour/egg; the Lumbridge basement has a bowl and sink. Wear ordinary leather gloves to pick up the hot rock cake, then kill an Ice Mountain icefiend to cool it. Ice gloves are a convenience here, not a new mandatory detour. Keep the dwarven rock cake afterwards.</li>
          <li><strong>Pirate Pete:</strong> empty fishbowl, needle, pestle and mortar, knife, <strong>3 bronze wire</strong>, raw cod and fresh bread. Smith three bronze bars into three wire at 4 Smithing (each bar is one copper + one tin); these are separate from Fenkenstrain's later three wires. Buy a big fishing net from Harry in Catherby and fish there for a raw cod at 23 Fishing if none remains. Murphy supplies the diving gear during the quest; keep it. Catch the underwater ingredients there, and replace cod/bread if the fishcake burns.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-fremennik" number="9" title="Complete The Fremennik Trials and Mountain Daughter">
        <p>Complete <strong>The Fremennik Trials</strong> from start to finish. Then complete <strong>Mountain Daughter</strong>. These quests establish the Fremennik foundation used heavily in later chapters.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Raw fish for the lyre and Mountain Daughter's crossing">
          <p><strong>The Fremennik Trials:</strong> bring 5,250 coins, tinderbox, knife, axe and <strong>1 raw shark, raw manta ray or raw sea turtle</strong>. Check the reward-fish bank first; if empty, buy one raw shark from <strong>Rufus's Meat Emporium in Canifis</strong> after Priest in Peril, or Frankie's Fishing Emporium in Port Piscarilius. Wait for stock or try another world if bought out. Do not cook this offering and do not grind 76 Fishing for it. The quest supplies the swaying-tree branch and golden fleece for your lyre; the local onion, cabbage and potato feed Lalli's stew. Check actual 25 Fletching/40 Woodcutting if making the lyre; these are below this route's established targets. Koschei's final form need not be defeated.</p>
          <p><strong>Mountain Daughter:</strong> 1 rope, pickaxe, axe, any plank, leather gloves and an elemental staff or the pole from the goat pen north of Hamal's tent. A dramen staff and vambraces do not satisfy the staff/gloves checks. Buy a normal plank from the sawmill by converting one ordinary log if none remains; keep food and your combat weapon for the Kendal.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-mory" number="10" title="Finish the Morytania prerequisites needed for the Farming quest chain">
        <p>Complete these as standalone quests:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Nature Spirit</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Shades of Mort'ton</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Creature of Fenkenstrain</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Plague City</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Silver check before these quests:</strong> Nature Spirit consumes one bar for the sickle, then Creature of Fenkenstrain consumes another for the conductor. Keep them separate from the bar already spent on Shadow of the Storm and the later holy-symbol/Desert Treasure allocations; if either is missing, refill at the East Ardougne Silver Merchant before its quest. Keep the <strong>ring of charos</strong> from Creature of Fenkenstrain; Garden of Tranquillity uses it in 1.4. From <strong>Plague City</strong>, also keep the <strong>gas mask</strong> in your bank. Desert Treasure's Smoke Dungeon requires a facemask, Slayer helmet or gas mask, so the quest reward already solves that requirement without another shopping trip. Plague City also leaves <strong>Biohazard</strong> ready to be completed cleanly later.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Sickle, serum, conductor and hangover-cure ingredients">
          <ul>
          <li><strong>Nature Spirit:</strong> ghostspeak amulet and silver sickle. Use one silver bar with a sickle mould bought from Dommik at a furnace (18 Crafting). Drezel and the quest supply the food, mirror and spell; finish with the blessed sickle and druid pouch retained.</li>
          <li><strong>Shades of Mort'ton:</strong> <strong>2 clean tarromin + 2 water-filled vials + 2 ashes</strong>, 1 normal log, tinderbox, hammer and about 5,000 coins for Razmire's local supplies. Read the book first, then make Serum 207 at 15 Herblore; these herbs are additional to the later Kourend diary's tarromin. Join the official Shades of Mort'ton world for temple repair, buy timber/limestone/swamp paste and olive oil in Mort'ton, sanctify the oil at the charged temple and use it on the log. The quest supplies the remains by killing a shade; you do not need a stock of higher pyre logs.</li>
          <li><strong>Creature of Fenkenstrain:</strong> ghostspeak amulet, hammer, spade, needle, <strong>5 thread, 3 new bronze wire, 1 new silver bar</strong>, 100 coins plus either Telekinetic Grab runes or another 50 coins for the pickled brain. Buy the brain from the Canifis pub if using coins. Smith the wires from three bronze bars; collect the body parts, garden cane and quest conductor mould during the quest. Keep the ring of charos.</li>
          <li><strong>Plague City:</strong> dwellberries, spade, rope, bucket of milk, chocolate dust and <strong>1 snape grass</strong>. Pick dwellberries in McGrubor's Wood, milk a Lumbridge dairy cow, crush a chocolate bar from the Grand Tree with a pestle and mortar, and pick snape grass on the hobgoblin peninsula west of the Crafting Guild. No Farming level or seed is needed. This grass is spent on the hangover cure; do not count it toward later prayer potions. Keep the gas mask.</li>
          </ul>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-fairy1" number="11" title="Complete Lost City, then Fairytale I">
        <p>Complete <strong>Lost City</strong>, then complete <strong>Fairytale I – Growing Pains</strong>. Bring the <strong>ghostspeak amulet</strong> banked in 1.1 when Quest Helper asks for it. The magic-secateurs phase assigns <strong>three account-specific items</strong>; read the actual request before sourcing them, then use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fairytale_I_-_Growing_Pains#Secateurs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current item-by-item source table</a> for the three rolled materials. They are a quest-specific branch, not three items the earlier random-reward bank can guarantee. Do not leave the quest at the request stage—complete it to collect the Farming XP below.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Why Fairytale I is here:</strong> it awards <strong>3,500 Farming XP</strong>. That is enough to clear the <strong>17 Farming</strong> requirement for Forgettable Tale even if you started with essentially no Farming XP.</div>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Lost City kit and the three items your account actually rolls">
          <p><strong>Lost City:</strong> reach actual 31 Crafting/36 Woodcutting, bring a knife, combat runes and food, and bank weapons/armour before boarding for Entrana. Kill the dungeon zombies for a bronze axe, use Magic from behind the mushrooms against the tree spirit, then cut dramen branches and knife them into staffs. Make one working staff and at least one spare for recovery; you cannot take a normal axe through the monks' equipment check.</p>
          <p><strong>Fairytale I:</strong> dramen staff, ghostspeak amulet, spade and secateurs from Sarah's farm shop south of Falador. Dig the Draynor skull from the grave north of the manor when asked. Read Malignius's <strong>actual three-item request</strong> before shopping; use the branch table below. Bring a filled druid pouch for edible items crossing Mort Myre: Bloom with the blessed sickle, collect extra swamp produce and fill the pouch without consuming a requested pear/stem/fungus.</p>
          <p><strong>Only collect your rolled items.</strong> They are not guaranteed by Wintertodt, and a high Farming or Herblore level is not the default solution:</p>
          <ul>
          <li><strong>White berries:</strong> kill chaos druid warriors in Yanille Agility Dungeon (40 Agility) for one; stay away from the chaos altar that drops you into poison spiders.</li>
          <li><strong>Mort myre pear / stem / fungus:</strong> Bloom with the blessed sickle beside a bush / branch / rotten log respectively; collect the required produce loose.</li>
          <li><strong>Nature talisman:</strong> if no reward/drop is banked, buy one for 50 abyssal pearls from Apprentice Felix at Guardians of the Rift after Temple of the Eye. If Temple of the Eye is unfinished, first reach 10 Runecraft (Enter the Abyss is already done; mine rune essence through Aubury and craft air runes at the altar south of Falador for the small remaining XP gap; if the air talisman is missing, kill the air wizard beside Malignius Mortifer north-west of Port Sarim until it drops one), then take a bucket of water, pickaxe and chisel to Wizard Persten north of Al Kharid and complete its tutorial. For normal rounds, enter the basement rift below the Wizards' Tower with pickaxe/chisel: mine guardian fragments, make guardian essence, craft at the active altars you can use, then deliver the resulting stones to the Great Guardian. Earn both elemental and catalytic energy, claim rewards and stop once the actual pearl balance reaches 50. This conditional unlock is only for a missing talisman; do not rely on fairy-ring Abyss access before Fairytale I.</li>
          <li><strong>Clean avantoe / irit leaf:</strong> get the grimy herb from banked drops or Taverley chaos druids; if below 48 / 40 Herblore, pay Zahur in Nardah 200 coins to clean the requested herb. Do not turn it into an unfinished potion.</li>
          <li><strong>Blue dragon scale:</strong> take an anti-dragon shield and pick a ground scale in Taverley Dungeon's blue-dragon chamber. If you do not have the shield yet, start Dragon Slayer I at the Champions' Guild and obtain it from Duke Horacio first. Below 70 Agility, free Velrak in the Black Knights' base for the dusty key. Bring antipoison, food and a teleport; no dragon kill is required.</li>
          <li><strong>Proboscis / volencia moss:</strong> do Jungle Potion now if either is rolled, then collect mosquito proboscis during Tai Bwo Wannai Cleanup or clean the moss from the jungle-mine rocks. This brings forward only that prerequisite; keep the later 31-Herblore check as a live level check and do not add Jungle Potion's XP twice.</li>
          <li><strong>Jangerberries / lime:</strong> use banked Hosidius fruit-stall produce; otherwise steal jangerberries there at 25 Thieving and buy a lime from the Grand Tree.</li>
          <li><strong>Potato cactus:</strong> take a rope, antipoison, food and a teleport to the Kalphite Lair west of Shantay Pass. Use the entrance rope and collect a ground potato cactus near the soldiers; no seed or 64 Farming is required.</li>
          <li><strong>Crushed gem / unopened oyster:</strong> pan at the Digsite for opals/oysters. Keep an oyster unopened. Cut spare opals with a chisel until one fails into a crushed gem; a cut opal is not a substitute.</li>
          <li><strong>Clean snapdragon:</strong> the Brimhaven Agility Arena sells one for 10 Brimhaven vouchers. At this route's 50+ Agility, tag consecutive active ticket dispensers until you have 10 Brimhaven vouchers, and buy one herb from Pirate Jackie the Fruit. This replaces an assumed high-level herb bank.</li>
          <li><strong>Supercompost:</strong> put 15 pineapples from a charter shop in an empty compost bin, close it, then return after rotting and take one bucket of supercompost. This is separate from Garden of Tranquillity's later reward.</li>
          <li><strong>Babydragon bones:</strong> kill a baby blue dragon in Taverley Dungeon; use the same dusty-key route as the scale. <strong>Jogre bones:</strong> kill a jogre in Pothole Dungeon on Karamja. These are specific bones, not ordinary or adult dragon bones.</li>
          <li><strong>Uncut diamond / uncut ruby:</strong> use banked uncut gems or the extra-stardust gem bags from Step 5, preserving the 2,000 ring reserve. Stop when the requested uncut stone appears; a cut gem will not work.</li>
          <li><strong>Raw cave eel / raw slimy eel:</strong> fishing rod and bait from Gerrant, plus a lit enclosed oil lantern, for Lumbridge Swamp Caves; 38 / 28 Fishing respectively. Enter through the Lost Tribe castle route and avoid cave hazards. Keep the fish raw. The lantern recipe is in the material-suppliers note.</li>
          <li><strong>Edible seaweed:</strong> pick the edible-seaweed spawn on Fossil Island's north-east coast; ordinary seaweed is different. <strong>Red vine worm:</strong> dig in McGrubor's Wood with a spade. <strong>Fat snail:</strong> kill a bruise or blood blamish snail in Mort Myre and keep its raw meat.</li>
          <li><strong>Charcoal:</strong> Jiminua's Jungle Store. <strong>Red spiders' eggs:</strong> ground spawns by the moss giants at the west end of Varrock Sewers, with a knife for webs. <strong>Grapes:</strong> the now-unlocked Culinaromancer's Chest. <strong>King worm:</strong> ground spawns north-west in the Gnome Stronghold. <strong>Snape grass:</strong> ground spawns west of the Crafting Guild.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>For Tanglefoot, equip the <strong>magic secateurs</strong>; ordinary weapons cannot finish this fight. Without 43 Prayer yet, use the mushroom/corridor flinch: hit once, return behind the obstacle and wait for its health bar to disappear before the next hit. Bring food for mistakes and bank the spare dramen staff in Zanaris.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-fairy2" number="12" title="Start Fairytale II only until fairy rings are unlocked">
        <p>Start <strong>Fairytale II – Cure a Queen</strong> and continue only until the <strong>Fairy Godfather gives you permission to use fairy rings</strong>. Stop there.</p>
        <p>This is one of the few intentional partial quests in the guide. Fairy rings are a major transport unlock, while finishing Fairytale II has much higher skill requirements. Keep a <strong>dramen staff</strong> available whenever a route step uses fairy rings.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supplies for the intended partial quest">
          <p>Bring the retained dramen staff. Martin's crop wait is real; if he asks you to return later, do another short activity. Collect Nuff's certificate in the quest and read the relevant notice/plaque when prompted. <strong>Stop at fairy-ring permission</strong>; the magic-essence ingredients and the quest's higher Herblore/Farming requirements belong to completion in Chapter 2.6, not this transport unlock.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-forgettable" number="13" title="Complete The Giant Dwarf, then complete Forgettable Tale">
        <p>Complete <strong>The Giant Dwarf</strong>. If its variable company errand asks for silver bars, buy those <em>in addition to</em> the remaining quest-reserved bars at the East Ardougne Silver Merchant rather than spending the Animal Magnetism/Desert Treasure stock. Then start <strong>Forgettable Tale...</strong> and begin the kelda brewing/fermentation step. The Rowdy dwarf's kelda-seed item request varies: ask what he wants, check the bank, and if that particular item is awkward tell him you do not know where to get it to request another item. Do not pre-bank a guessed universal item. Fermentation is a real timer, so this is the one place where leaving a quest waiting is intentional.</p>
        <p>Use the wait for a birdhouse run, a Crafting/Fletching session, or another finished activity. Return when the brew is ready and <strong>finish Forgettable Tale completely</strong>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Farming dependency solved:</strong> The Goblin generals subquest gave <strong>1,000 Farming XP</strong>, Fairytale I gives <strong>3,500</strong>, and Forgettable Tale gives <strong>5,000</strong>. That is <strong>9,500 Farming XP</strong> before the Zeah block, already enough for <strong>26 Farming</strong>. The Garden of Death later in this subsection adds another <strong>10,000 Farming XP</strong>, so 1.4 begins with at least <strong>19,500 XP (level 33)</strong>. Garden of Tranquillity therefore has no hidden Farming grind.</div>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Keldagrim errands and the complete kelda brewing kit">
          <p><strong>The Giant Dwarf:</strong> bring at least 2,500 coins plus a purchase buffer, a log, tinderbox, 1 coal, 1 iron bar, 3 cut sapphires, 1 law + 1 air rune for Telekinetic Grab, and a fresh redberry pie for Thurgo unless you already gave him an extra. Ordan sells coal/ore, the city jeweller sells cut sapphires, and a furnace turns iron ore into an iron bar at 15 Smithing. Bake the pie from flour/water/pie dish/redberries at 10 Cooking. Company errands request variable ores and bars: accept the task, buy its ore from Ordan and smelt any requested bars at the relevant Smithing level, then return before the timer expires. Let an awkward high-tier request expire and ask again; do not spend protected quest silver or manufacture a fixed universal ore list.</p>
          <p><strong>Forgettable Tale:</strong> 500 coins, 2 barley malt, 2 buckets of water, rake, seed dibber, 1 kebab, 3 beers, 1 dwarven stout and an empty beer glass, plus the actual Rowdy dwarf request. The Keldagrim food shop sells the kebab, its pubs sell beer, and a stout spawns beside the Drunken Dwarf; drinking a spare beer supplies the glass. If the two barley malt are missing, buy four barley seeds from Olivia in Draynor, plant them in the hops patch north of Lumbridge's cow field with a rake/seed dibber, and use compost/water. At 3+ Farming, harvest the mature barley and cook two on a range to make malt; plain barley does not work. This short crop is a quest ingredient, not a general Farming grind. The quest gives all four kelda seeds; grow them in its special patch, harvest the kelda hops, then add the two waters, two barley malt, hops and yeast to the brewing vat (take the nearby empty pot and pay Blandebir 25 coins for the yeast). Keep the empty glass to draw the finished beer. Wait until the vat is ready before drawing it; starting the timer does not mean the stout is already in your bank.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-troll" number="14" title="Complete Death Plateau and Troll Stronghold">
        <p>Complete <strong>Death Plateau</strong>, then complete <strong>Troll Stronghold</strong>. Buy and bank <strong>5 extra pairs of climbing boots</strong> while the shop access is convenient. During Troll Stronghold, make sure you <strong>free Eadgar</strong> and unlock the southern shortcut/entrance.</p>
        <p>These quests are direct prerequisites for <strong>Eadgar's Ruse</strong> and <strong>Desert Treasure</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Death Plateau's food order and the Troll Stronghold fight">
          <p><strong>Death Plateau:</strong> 60 coins, 1 premade Blurberry special, 1 iron bar, <strong>10 unnoted bread and 10 unnoted cooked trout</strong>. Buy the premade drink from Blurberry's Grand Tree bar; ordinary beer is not a replacement for this item. Steal bread at the Ardougne bakery stall or bake it; fly-fish and cook ten trout at Barbarian Village if the Fishing stock is gone. Smith the iron bar from mined/bought iron ore at 15 Smithing, allowing for failed smelts. These supplies are separate from later spiked boots and quest food.</p>
          <p><strong>Troll Stronghold:</strong> wear climbing boots; buy a replacement from Tenzing for 12 coins if needed. Bring combat runes, food and a bank teleport for Dad and the guards; use the arena fence to keep Dad away while casting. Protection prayers are helpful if already unlocked, but this chapter has not yet guaranteed 43 Prayer. Buy the five spare boot pairs after Death Plateau; one later becomes Desert Treasure's spiked boots.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-herblore" number="15" title="Reach 31 Herblore before leaving the Troll quest block">
        <p>If Herblore is below <strong>31</strong>, use banked Wintertodt herbs and simple potions to reach 31 now. <strong>Serum 207, compost potions, energy potions and restore potions</strong> are all reasonable fillers depending on your secondaries. Wintertodt herbs are random, not guaranteed: if the bank is short, kill <strong>Chaos druids in Taverley Dungeon</strong> (no Wilderness trip) for grimy low-level herbs, clean them and make only the live XP remainder. Bring combat gear, food, vials of water and a teleport; drops vary, so stop on <strong>actual 31</strong>, not a promised kill count. Tarromin plus ordinary ashes makes Serum 207 at 15 Herblore; at 26, harralander plus chocolate dust makes energy potions (Funch's Fine Groceries in the Grand Tree stocks chocolate bars). Keep one harralander back for Heroes' Quest.</p>
        <p>Training the level outright keeps the next subsection self-contained: <strong>Eadgar's Ruse requires 31 Herblore to start and to make the troll truth potion</strong>, so no temporary boost or separately sourced botanical pie is needed.</p>
        <div class="later-note"><strong>Do not use the last harralander.</strong> Put <strong>1 harralander</strong> aside in the bank specifically for <strong>Heroes' Quest</strong> in early Chapter 2; it is mixed with blamish snail slime and water to make the oil for the lava-eel fishing rod.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-karamja" number="16" title="Complete Jungle Potion and secure 60% favour for My Arm">
        <p>Complete <strong>Jungle Potion</strong> if not already finished for Fairytale I. Then bring a <strong>machete, antipoison, food and basic melee-defence gear</strong> to <strong>Tai Bwo Wannai Cleanup</strong>; switch auto-retaliate off. Hack jungle and handle the resulting encounters, or kill the local jungle spiders if you prefer, until your favour reaches <strong>at least 60%</strong>. My Arm's Big Adventure spends 60 percentage points; this is the actual mandatory consumer. Stop here if you are not deliberately pursuing the diary.</p>
        <div class="optional-efficiency"><strong>Optional Karamja Medium preparation:</strong> that diary also asks for <strong>100% favour</strong> and a <strong>regular gout tuber</strong> for the gem-machete exchange, but no Chapter 1–2 page completes the diary or spends its reward. If you want it later, continue Cleanup to 100% before My Arm and hunt the tuber using the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Gout_tuber/Strategies" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki dense-jungle/snake-boxing method</a>; bank it with a spade when its unusual plant appears. The drop is random and averages around an hour or more, so do not make it a hidden route gate. This <em>regular</em> tuber is distinct from the <em>hardy</em> quest tuber Murcaily gives during My Arm.</div>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Jungle Potion and the 60% Cleanup stop">
          <p><strong>Jungle Potion</strong> supplies its own five herbs from the jungle locations after Trufitus tells you what to find. Bring food and antipoison for the spiders. Jiminua's Jungle Store north-west of the village sells <strong>antipoison(3)</strong>, a machete and other basics, so an early herb/secondary grind is unnecessary. For Cleanup, buy the machete there, cut light jungle and repair the village fence; handle or avoid spawned enemies, check favour with a villager, and stop at <strong>60%</strong>. If the quest was completed early for Fairytale I's random items, do not count its XP again here.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-grail" number="17" title="Complete Holy Grail">
        <p>Complete <strong>Holy Grail</strong> as a standalone quest. Merlin's Crystal is already finished, so there is no quest-chain bookkeeping left to do here.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Excalibur and a prayer-independent Black Knight Titan plan">
          <p>Withdraw the <strong>Excalibur</strong> from Merlin's Crystal; if lost, recover it from the Lady of the Lake south-east of Taverley before travelling. The holy table napkin and magic whistle are obtained during the quest. Bring food, a teleport and your normal weapon, but use Excalibur for the Titan's finishing blow. If protection prayers are still locked, flinch the stationary Titan: hit, step out of reach, wait for the health bar to disappear, repeat. The optional melee detour in 1.4 has not happened yet.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-zeah" number="18" title="Do the Zeah quest block — but finish each quest before starting the next">
        <p>Zeah is the one area where several quests are worth grouping because they share the same travel network. Keep the geographic cluster, but finish each quest before beginning the next. Complete these <strong>one at a time</strong>, rebanking whenever useful:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>The Queen of Thieves</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Depths of Despair</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Forsaken Tower</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Tale of the Righteous</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Garden of Death</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Ascent of Arceuus</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Getting Ahead</strong></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Woodcutting Guild supply stop:</strong> while this Zeah block has you moving through Hosidius, stop at <strong>Perry’s Chop-chop Shop</strong> if you have reached <strong>60 Woodcutting</strong>. Buy a <strong>rune axe for 40,960 gp</strong> and use it for the long Woodcutting block in 1.4. If Wintertodt gave you the very rare <strong>dragon axe</strong>, you can skip the rune axe. Also buy and bank a cheap <strong>mithril axe</strong>; the Ranged block in <strong>1.4</strong> now completes <strong>Animal Magnetism</strong> before the long crab grind, so this prevents a return trip.</div>
        <p><strong>If you are still below 60 Woodcutting here:</strong> do not interrupt the quest block just to force the level. Keep using the steel axe for now. During the 1.4 Woodcutting break, reach 60, enter the Woodcutting Guild, buy the rune axe (and mithril axe), then continue toward 70. The guild itself requires 60 Woodcutting; the rune axe only requires 41 Woodcutting to chop with once you own it.</p>
        <p>Unlock the <strong>Mount Quidamortem mountain-guide shortcut</strong> when The Tale of the Righteous takes you there. That is a worthwhile permanent travel unlock rather than an incidental diary click.</p>
        <p><strong>Before leaving the bank:</strong> check the quest-specific quantities and sources in the preparation note.</p>
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supplies for every quest in the Zeah block">
          <ul>
          <li><strong>The Queen of Thieves:</strong> 1 stew. Buy a cooked stew from the Seers' Village pub or Warriors' Guild food shop if accessible; the Seers' pub needs no guild entry. Keep it for the quest instead of eating it.</li>
          <li><strong>The Depths of Despair:</strong> no outside quest item; bring combat gear, food and a teleport for the Sand Snake. Its scrolls/key are quest-local.</li>
          <li><strong>The Forsaken Tower:</strong> no outside ingredient; collect the building's tools and puzzle materials during the quest. No pre-banked potion recipe is needed.</li>
          <li><strong>Tale of the Righteous:</strong> pickaxe, rope, a ranged weapon with matching ammunition and runes for a combat spell. Bring both ranged and Magic even if you normally melee; one stack of iron knives plus air/mind runes for Wind Strike is a simple low-level kit.</li>
          <li><strong>The Garden of Death:</strong> secateurs, obtainable inside the quest or reused from Sarah's shop. Bring food for the surrounding creatures; the tablets and notes are collected along the route.</li>
          <li><strong>The Ascent of Arceuus:</strong> no outside quest ingredient; take combat gear, food and a teleport for the trapped souls.</li>
          <li><strong>Getting Ahead:</strong> actual 26 Construction, bear fur, 1 soft clay, hammer, saw, <strong>2 normal planks, at least 6 nails</strong> (take spares), knife, red dye, flour, needle and thread. The farm supplies the construction/crafting materials when searched; kill a bear west of it for fur. Use those local supplies before buying duplicates, and take any free replacement nails if some bend.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Finish and retain the Kharedst's memoirs pages as each quest awards them. If a later teleport is depleted, recharge the book at the Old Memorial using the required runes; an unlocked destination does not guarantee remaining charges.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i13-finish" number="19" title="Verify the 1.3 handoff before taking the Woodcutting break">
        <p>Before moving to 1.4, confirm:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Bones to Peaches</strong> unlocked</li>
          <li><strong>44 Mining / actual 46+ Crafting / 46+ Fletching</strong> — 46 Crafting allows the orb batch, which may still be underway here; 1.4 checks actual 49 before The Hand in the Sand and postpones the 58-or-pie decision until after quest rewards. Do not grind 48 Fletching just to match BRUHsailer's projected stat.</li>
          <li><strong>1,590 unpowered orbs</strong> completed, or actively being chipped away at with the explicit deadline to finish them before Earth-orb charging in 1.4</li>
          <li><strong>7 molten glass</strong> protected from the orb stack: 6 for Desert Treasure and 1 for The Hand in the Sand; one glass built crafting table 2 and up to two remain spare (one may already be Pirate Pete's fishbowl). Keep at least one molten glass for Chapter 2.</li>
          <li><strong>2,000 stardust</strong> banked and unspent for the Celestial ring</li>
          <li><strong>Rune sword + green d'hide chaps/vambraces</strong> banked/equipped</li>
          <li><strong>Axe upgrade accounted for:</strong> if you already have 60 Woodcutting, <strong>rune axe</strong> obtained for normal Woodcutting (unless you got a dragon axe) and <strong>1 mithril axe</strong> banked for Animal Magnetism in 1.4. If you are still below 60, these are explicitly deferred to the moment you hit 60 in the opening 1.4 Woodcutting break.</li>
          <li><strong>Birdhouse runs</strong> available; first <strong>2 teak seeds</strong> reserved when obtained</li>
          <li><strong>Fairy rings</strong> available</li>
          <li><strong>Forgettable Tale</strong> and <strong>The Garden of Death</strong> complete, leaving at least <strong>33 Farming</strong></li>
          <li><strong>The Fremennik Trials</strong> complete</li>
          <li><strong>Death Plateau + Troll Stronghold</strong> complete</li>
          <li><strong>Creature of Fenkenstrain</strong> complete with the ring of charos banked</li>
          <li><strong>60% Tai Bwo Wannai favour</strong> ready for My Arm; 100% and a regular gout tuber are optional diary preparation</li>
          <li><strong>100+ Varrock Museum Kudos</strong> and <strong>Bone Voyage</strong> complete</li>
          <li><strong>26+ Construction</strong> and <strong>Getting Ahead</strong> complete</li>
          <li><strong>1 harralander</strong> reserved for Heroes' Quest; keep another four unprocessed for DT restores if available (the DT step supplies a missing-stock recovery)</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout"><strong>1.3 complete:</strong> the next subsection deliberately opens with a long, simple Woodcutting break before returning to quests.</div>
      </RouteStep>

